Apple is expected to replace the LCD screens in both sizes of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/">iPad Air</a> with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> displays in the first half of 2027, according to <a href="https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261110PD211/apple-sdc-2027-ipad-air-panel.html"><em>DigiTimes</em></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/03/m3-ipad-air-blue.jpeg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-996101" /><br/>
An &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; has been rumored for over a year. <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/28/apple-ipad-macbook-oled-displays/">reported in October 2025</a> that Apple was developing one and that it was unlikely to arrive before 2027. He <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/01/three-new-ipads-in-first-half-of-2027/">narrowed that window</a> to the first half of 2027 earlier this month. The latest report adds shipment estimates and details on how panel orders could be split.<br/>
<br/>
Samsung Display is expected to supply most &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; panels. BOE is <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/11/ipad-air-oled-panel-orders-could-be-split-with-boe/">seeking orders</a> for one of the two sizes and still needs to qualify as a supplier. With orders for the &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a>, Samsung could become Apple's largest supplier of &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> panels overall, while LG Display is expected to retain the lead for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-pro/">iPad Pro</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Industry estimates cited by <em><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/digitimes-com/">DigiTimes</a></em> put 2027 shipments at 4 million to 5 million units each for the &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPad mini&zwnj;, and 3 million to 4 million for the &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj;. The &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj; estimates each cover both screen sizes. The &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj; forecast is well below its reported pre-launch target of around 10 million units per year, with industry sources pointing to the price as a factor in weaker demand.<br/>
<br/>
Both sizes of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/02/apple-announces-ipad-air-with-m4-chip/">current M4 iPad Air</a> use LCD screens. The move to &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; would make the &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; Apple's third &zwnj;iPad&zwnj; line to adopt the technology, following the &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj; in 2024 and the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/27/oled-ipad-mini-pre-orders-and-release-date/">8.5-inch iPad mini</a> that went on sale November 6.<br/>
<br/>
According to <em>&zwnj;DigiTimes&zwnj;</em>, the &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; is expected to use the same single-stack &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; design and low-temperature polycrystalline silicon (LTPS) backplane as the &zwnj;iPad mini&zwnj;. The &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj; uses two light-emitting stacks to boost brightness and reportedly uses a low-temperature polycrystalline oxide (LTPO) backplane.<br/>
<br/>
LTPO's oxide transistors help pixels hold their charge longer between refreshes, so the display can save power by refreshing less often when the image is still. The &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj;'s ProMotion display can vary its refresh rate from 10Hz to 120Hz. <em>&zwnj;DigiTimes&zwnj;</em> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/20/five-apple-products-to-get-oled-displays/">previously reported</a> that the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; would stick with 60Hz, leaving ProMotion exclusive to the &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj; in Apple's tablet lineup.<div class="linkback">Related Roundup: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/">iPad Air </a></div><div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/digitimes-com/">DigiTimes</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/oled/">OLED</a></div><div class="linkback">Buyer's Guide: <a href="https://buyersguide.macrumors.com/#iPad-Air">iPad Air (Neutral)</a></div><div class="linkback">Related Forum: <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/ipad.137">iPad</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/10/oled-ipad-air-rumored-to-launch-in-early-2027/">OLED iPad Air Rumored to Launch in Two Sizes in Early 2027</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/oled-ipad-air-rumored-to-launch-in-two-sizes-in-early-2027.2494090/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>